  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between isochlorogenic acid A and Leukocyte antigen CD37, as the compound is implicated in targeting multiple pathways that ultimately lead to the CD37 protein. Specifically, isochlorogenic acid A is shown to interact with NCI-H2347, which is a target of several compounds, including 3-Hydroxymandelic acid, (-) and (3Beta,24R)-Stigmasta-5,28-Diene-3,24-Diol. These compounds, in turn, are targets of CD37, indicating a chain of molecular interactions that may be relevant to the biological function of CD37. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The evidence highlights the importance of these intermediates in the pathway leading to CD37, but further experimental validation is needed to establish a direct interaction between isochlorogenic acid A and CD37.",
